216| * fallbacks of their own. The child is pinned to a `subagent:<id>` role whose
217| * chain shadows every configured role chain (see
218| * {@link installSubagentRetryFallbackChain}), so a role-alias request (`@smol`,
219| * the bundled `task` agent's `@task`) MUST inherit that role's chain —
220| * otherwise the pin silently re-routes the child onto the `default` role's
221| * chain. Explicit model selectors keep inheriting `default`: they carry no role
222| * identity, and a role that happens to be assigned the same model must not
223| * capture the child's fallback routing.
